  "raw": " Casselton on Aug. 19, 1955.\nHe attended Goodman Elementary School and graduated from Twin Valley High School. He earned a bachelor's degree in applied science from West Virginia University. Following graduation, Flip received membership in the United States Army Reserves and remained active until his retirement in September 2015.\nFlip enjoyed outdoor activities but what he truly loved more than anything were his two children and grandchildren.\nSurviving are his wife of 41 years, Denise; one son, Tyler (Stephanie); one daughter, Troya Roloff; and one granddaughter, Darcy Joan.\nFuneral services will be at 2 p.m. Wednesday at Goodwin Funeral Home and Crematory, Goodman. Inurnment will follow at Nicholson Cemetery.\nThe family requests that those attending wear masks and maintain social distancing while in the funeral home.\nMemorial contributions may be made to St. Jude Children's Research Hospital or the Prostate Cancer Foundation, 1701 Walnut",
  "serialized": "Casselton on Aug. 19, 1955. He attended Goodman Elementary School and graduated from Twin Valley High School. He earned a bachelor's degree in applied science from West Virginia University. Following graduation, Flip received membership in the United States Army Reserves and remained active until his retirement in September 2015. Flip enjoyed outdoor activities but what he truly loved more than anything were his two children and grandchildren. Surviving are his wife of 41 years, Denise; one son, Tyler (Stephanie); one daughter, Troya Roloff; and one granddaughter, Darcy Joan. Funeral services will be at 2 p.m. Wednesday at Goodwin Funeral Home and Crematory, Goodman. Inurnment will follow at Nicholson Cemetery. The family requests that those attending wear masks and maintain social distancing while in the funeral home. Memorial contributions may be made to St. Jude Children's Research Hospital or the Prostate Cancer Foundation, 1701 Walnut",
